{title: Quemadmodum Desiderat Cervus}
{subtitle: Psalms 42:2–4}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As a deer longs for [Bb]streams of [Eb]water
[Cm]So my soul longs for [Bb]you, O [Eb]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My [Ab]soul thirsts for [Bb]God, [Gm]for the living [Cm]God
[Ab]When shall I [Bb]come and appear [Ab]before God's [Eb]face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My [Bb]tears have [Cm]been my [Ab]food day and [Eb]night
While [Bb]all day [Cm]long they [Ab]say to [Bb]me, Where is your [Ab]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
For [Bb]you, O [Eb]God
{end_of_verse}
